# HG2-A (VIS): `late` is declared before its use: in delayed() before the branch (the branch-local name is not visible outside, #call-frame-20261115 para 5); in cleanup() as a field of the header data, because `cleanup\data\late` is read below. A write to the bare late is the call's local, and the finally writes it explicitly (rule Б: data\late := late + 1), so after 5 (pin kept). Observation: the root values are written explicitly in sub: observe (#flush-receiver-contract; #call-frame-20261115).
(
    Observed:
        int: result 0
        int: held 0
        int: after 0
        int: fields 0
)
@: shared data[0]
fn: delayed () int
    int: late 0
    if: 0 ()
    else: (late := 7)
    return: late
fn: cleanup () int (int: late 0)
    late := 4
    finally: (int: late; data\late := late + 1)
    return: late
sub: inert () ()
    if: 0 ()
    else: ((int: phantom 7; missing()))
int: result delayed()
int: held cleanup()
int: after cleanup\data\late
inert()
int: fields length(inert\data)

sub: observe ()
    shared\Observed\result := result
    shared\Observed\held := held
    shared\Observed\after := after
    shared\Observed\fields := fields
observe()
